{"title":"Vertex","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertex_(curve)\" title=\"Vertex (curve)\">Vertex (curve)</a> - The <b>vertex</b> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parabola\" title=\"Parabola\">parabola</a> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Midpoint\" title=\"Midpoint\">midpoint</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line_segment\" title=\"Line segment\">line segment</a> joining the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Focus\" title=\"Focus\">focus</a> of the parabola to the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Directrix\" title=\"Directrix\">directrix</a> that is perpendicular to the directrix.  This line is the line of symmetry of the parabola.  If the parabola lies in a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cartesian_coordinate_system\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cartesian coordinate system\">Cartesian coordinate system</a> as the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Graph_of_a_function\" title=\"Graph of a function\"> graph</a> of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/878740b1e9bad0008122348eca48d8883a00e7ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = ax^2 + bx + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /> then this line is vertical and the vertex is the point at which the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-value of the graph is minimal (if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25634d7212302efdeb3702974863759bfb74d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />) or maximal (if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/1/c319a78bbce71ba12b4ccb52f0b0b793ef760f58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />).</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertex_(geometry)\" title=\"Vertex (geometry)\">Vertex (geometry)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertex_(graph_theory)&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Vertex (graph theory) (page does not exist)\">Vertex (graph theory)</a></li>\n<li>Note that <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertices\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Vertices\">vertices</a> is the plural form of vertex.</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<p><i>This is a disambiguation page.  The title you requested could refer to one of the articles listed on this page.</i>\n</p><p>If you were referred to this page through an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Special:WhatLinksHere/Vertex\" title=\"Special:WhatLinksHere/Vertex\">internal link</a> and you believe that a direct link to a specific article would be more appropriate, feel free to help us out by changing the link on that page.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Vertex&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018113547\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.025 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 22/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 655/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 714/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   10.747      1 -total\n 51.79%    5.566      1 Template:Disambig\n 46.93%    5.043      1 Template:Stub\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1829:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018113547 and revision id 243688. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}